s11-p5 : Block
s11-p5 = prose (cons "A description need not be frozen when its subject changes. Guarded interactions keep processes open; recorded read dependencies say when retained computations still apply; effect histories constrain restarts; content-addressed definitions and their evidence can be inspected and exchanged by participants without a global interpreter of their meaning. This makes the continuing activity of description, inference, and transformation itself available to computation. The result is a language for nature that includes the work of understanding nature, and an executable environment in which that work can act on its own products. This returns to the scientific horizon of *A New Kind of Science* ([64](#ref-64)): the universe and the activity of investigating it are both within the subject of computation. *Hyperactivity* names the activity, not a separate layer standing over it." nil)
